<h2 id=3D"run-locally">Running Coder-Next on Your Own Hardware</h2>
<p>
  The MoE architecture makes this model far more accessible than its 80B pa=
rameter count suggests. The key metric isn't GPU VRAM alone =E2=80=94 it's =
<strong>total system memory</strong> (RAM + VRAM combined). Most users run =
the GGUF quantizations through llama.cpp, Ollama, or LM Studio. Want to che=
ck if your specific setup can handle it? Use our <a href=3D"https://qwen-ai=
.com/can-i-run-qwen/">Can I Run Qwen?</a> tool.
</p>

